.Sh DESCRIPTION
This command processes CRL files in DER or PEM format.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy -help
Print out a usage message.
.It Sy -inform Sy DER Ns | Ns Sy PEM
The CRL input format; unspecified by default.
See
.Xr openssl-format-options 1
for details.
.It Sy -outform Sy DER Ns | Ns Sy PEM
The CRL output format; the default is
.Sy PEM .
See
.Xr openssl-format-options 1
for details.
.It Sy -key Em filename
The private key to be used to sign the CRL.
.It Sy -keyform Sy DER Ns | Ns Sy PEM Ns | Ns Sy P12
The format of the private key file; unspecified by default.
See
.Xr openssl-format-options 1
for details.
.It Sy -in Em filename
This specifies the input filename to read from or standard input if this
option is not specified.
.It Sy -out Em filename
Specifies the output filename to write to or standard output by default.
.It Sy -gendelta Em filename
Output a comparison of the main CRL and the one specified here.
.It Sy -badsig
Corrupt the signature before writing it; this can be useful for testing.
.It Sy -dateopt
Specify the date output format.
Values are: rfc_822 and iso_8601. Defaults to rfc_822.
.It Sy -text
Print out the CRL in text form.
.It Sy -verify
Verify the signature in the CRL. If the verification fails, the program
will immediately exit, i.e.
further option processing (e.g.
.Sy -gendelta )
is skipped.
.Pp
This option is implicitly enabled if any of
.Sy -CApath ,
.Sy -CAfile
or
.Sy -CAstore
is specified.
.It Sy -noout
Don't output the encoded version of the CRL.
.It Sy -fingerprint
Output the fingerprint of the CRL.
.It Sy -crlnumber
Output the number of the CRL.
.It Sy -hash
Output a hash of the issuer name.
This can be use to lookup CRLs in a directory by issuer name.
.It Sy -hash_old
Outputs the "hash" of the CRL issuer name using the older algorithm as
used by OpenSSL before version 1.0.0.
.It Sy -issuer
Output the issuer name.
.It Sy -lastupdate
Output the lastUpdate field.
.It Sy -nextupdate
Output the nextUpdate field.
.It Sy -nameopt Em option
This specifies how the subject or issuer names are displayed.
See
.Xr openssl-namedisplay-options 1
for details.
.It Sy -CAfile Em file Ns , Sy -no-CAfile Ns , Sy -CApath Em dir Ns , Sy -no-CApath Ns , Sy -CAstore Em uri Ns , Sy -no-CAstore
See
.Xr openssl-verification-options 1
for details.
.It Sy -provider Em name
.It Sy -provider-path Em path
.It Sy -provparam Em [name:]key=value
.It Sy -propquery Em propq
See
.Xr openssl 1 ,
.Xr provider 7 ,
and
.Xr property 7 .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Convert a CRL file from PEM to DER:
.Bd -literal
 openssl crl -in crl.pem -outform DER -out crl.der
.Ed
.Pp
Output the text form of a DER encoded certificate:
.Bd -literal
 openssl crl -in crl.der -text -noout
.Ed
.Sh BUGS
Ideally it should be possible to create a CRL using appropriate options
and files too.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr openssl 1 ,
